const e=JSON.parse(`[{"id":"s01","number":1,"title":"The start of something new","img":"/images/sesh1.png","date":"2026-01-04","summary":"A twisted fate awaited the party as they awoke amidst the rubble of what had once been the Silver Chalice. Shattered beams and broken stone told the story of sudden destruction, the work of a young dragon, its mind possessed by chaos.\\n\\n\\nWithin moments, Waess noticed something was wrong. The dragon was sick. Without hesitation, he chose survival over confrontation, setting his sights on escape and rushing to bring himself to safety.\\n\\n\\nRay, however, had other plans. Spotting a seemingly injured figure lying helplessly on the ground, he shot an arrow at the dragon, successfully drawing its attention away from the victim. \\nThe dragon’s gaze shifted and then it noticed Waess attempting to flee.\\n\\n\\nWith a powerful beat of its wings, the dragon took off and struck Waess down, knocking him unconscious. Ray sprinted toward Waess’s fallen body, desperately trying to check on him. He placed himself between Waess's unconscious body and the dragon, standing as a shield.\\n\\n\\nThe dragon struck Ray with the same brutal force, leaving him collpased on the ground beside Waess.\\n\\n\\nAmidst the chaos, Marvers focused on what he could still save. He moved through the wreckage, helping as many survivors as possible. His efforts failed at the last person, a woman with a broken leg, barely able to suppress her pain filled whimpers.\\n\\n\\nThe dragon quickly noticed.\\n\\n\\nIt lunged toward Marvers and sank its teeth into his shoulder, attempting to finish him off right where he stood.\\n\\n\\n“Just when it seems that all hope is lost, the three of you feel a sudden warmth, a resonance within the items that have guided your journey so far. Light bursts from each of your \\"special\\" items. Marvers’s holy symbol, Ray’s bolotie and Waess’s moon necklace. You begin to float off the ground, the light swirling around you, merging into a blinding magical explosion that shakes the Inn to its foundations.”\\n\\n\\nEveryone wakes up in the Monastery located on the very top of Guardians Height.\\n\\n\\nWaess and Ray talked things out regarding the attack right after they awoke, while Marvers checked on Martin and his newly found friend. Martin, worried, asked Marvers to find out whether his grandmother Lilia was safe.\\n\\n\\nAfterward, Waess struck up a conversation with Aarely. And through him, Marvers discovered that they shared the same religion.\\n\\n\\nRay headed to the Main Hall to speak with Berta, a nun who lived in the monastery, about the deity Talona and this mysterious Person called Misha. During their conversation, he learned that Talona has an active temple in Duweil. Berta sent a messenger to a priest who was close to Misha to gather more information about her whereabouts.\\n\\n\\nMeanwhile, Marvers and Waess went to a small and diy'd temple (probably by Aarley) to pray to Soldea. Both of them individually prayed, received a subtle sign in response and then left. On their way back, Waess discovered a small note from Wilfen, written in Elvish using expensive purple ink. \\"Whoever can read this, Hello there :)\\"\\n\\n\\nLater, Ray went to the gardens by himself to inform Erwin (in his head) that everything was alright. While there, he too received a small sign making him feel assured that he is going to be alright, everything is going to be alright..","highlights":["The Party meets","Encounter with a Dragon"],"npcs":["Aarely"],"locations":["Lacrima","Guardians Height"]},{"id":"s02","number":2,"title":"Leaving Guardians Height behind","img":"/images/sesh3.png","date":"2026-01-09","summary":"The group found themselves still within the monastery. After Ray briefly left Waess and Marvers to explore the gardens, the two decided to further inspect the murals lining the monastery’s walls. Marvers noticed several explicit sexual depictions, including one portraying the three rulers of Lacrima, Duweil and Dredel engaged in intercourse, accompanied by an elvish inscription reading “Fuck Capitalism.” Marvers was deeply confused as to why such imagery was permitted on holy grounds.\\n\\nMeanwhile, Waess cast Redraw and Rewrite, causing the letters of Wiltfen’s message to dance and transform into small, stick-like figures. He also commented that Marvers’ “Spine tale”, an element of Ivian culture seemed unusually short for his age. Marvers bluntly shut the conversation down, making it clear he did not wish to discuss it.\\n\\nWhen Ray returned, he and Waess set off together with two goals: to find Aarely and to get Ray to a post office. On their way toward the monastery’s main entrance, the two shared a surprisingly intimate conversation, ending in Waess offering himself should Ray ever wish to explore intimacy with another man. The moment was abruptly interrupted by a passing monk. They asked him for directions to Aarely and the post office, then parted ways.\\n\\nWhile this was happening, Marvers returned to the room left to where they had first awakened. After knocking, he heard a hushed “enter”and slowly opened the door to complete darkness. As he stepped inside, the door slammed shut behind him and a hand gripped his shoulder, startling him. Once his eyes adjusted, he saw a tall high elf, nearly his height, standing close behind him.\\n\\nThe elf seized Marvers arm and pulled him toward the altar, where he cast light on a wooden handle and pointed to a book. He wrote a single question: \\"What are you looking for?” Upon closer inspection, Marvers noticed how unsettling the elf appeared, long, straight black hair perfectly arranged down his back, a slim face, and a prominent scar running across his left eye. One eye was milky white, the other a piercing grey.\\n\\nAfter a brief interaction, the elf guided Marvers out of the room, still holding his hand. As they left, Marvers caught a glimpse of someone lying in the darkness, a person with a fatal looking wound that did not bleed. Instead, the injury appeared grown over with grey, ashen wood. The figure made no sound, yet Marvers was convinced they were still alive. Shaken, he paused to steady himself before continuing his search for Layla.\\n\\nElsewhere, Waess found Aarely and pulled him out of an impending burnout by guilting him into joining Waess for a meal. They sat down at a small restaurant consisting of a bar counter and three tables, where they ate Meadowroot and Griftlon stew, a dish similar to one from Lacrima, though made with Griftlon meat (a large mountain bird) instead of rabbit. During the meal, Aarely revealed that his deity had sent him a sign: the group needed to leave the monastery as soon as possible.\\n\\nRay, meanwhile, made his way to the post office. There, he befriended the postal worker Matteo and struck a deal, informing Sir Halden about the mysterious letters he had been receiving and agreeing to write Matteo about the outcome.\\n\\nAfter searching the entire monastery without success, Marvers entered the main hall, where he spoke with Berta. From her, he learned that Layla may have already been healed and released. He also uncovered grim historical knowledge: roughly 150 years ago, Queen Cyria Powsky ordered the eradication of all remaining dragons, resulting in a widespread witch hunt situation in which any being suspected of being a dragon was executed. \\nWhen the group finally reunited, Aarely informed Marvers that Layla was in the Darkroom and infected. He instructed Ray to leave with the group, promising to deliver the priests reply as soon as possible.\\n\\nOn their way to the gate, Marvers put on his armor, revealing the King’s family crest once worn by Lacrima’s soldiers. The group quickly concealed it with Marvers scarf before proceeding. At the gate, they encountered Virex Halden, who offered to let them leave the village in exchange for interrogating them. As part of the deal, they were also to report what they had witnessed to a nearby Lacriman outpost.\\n\\nEach member of the party was asked the same question. Afterward, Virex released them, just as Aarely arrived. He warned them quietly:\\n\\n“Be careful. I hope to see you again soon. She who watches me from afar has shown me that no good comes from sharing the whole truth with those who serve Lacrima. Not telling is not lying. Be careful out there.”\\n\\nAnd with that, the party made their way onward.\\n","highlights":["Encountering Virex Halden","Seeing the weird Sickness unfold"],"npcs":["Virex Halden, Aarely"],"locations":["Lacrima","Guardians Height"]},{"id":"s03","number":3,"title":"A warm welcome by Commander Halden","img":"/images/sesh2.png","date":"2026-01-20","summary":"The party made their way down from Guardians’ Height after the first interrogation with Commander Virex Halden. The hike took about four hours, and by approximately 3PM, they began making their way through the forest.\\n\\nWaesstan confronted Marvers about his suspicious behavior and expressed his concerns regarding Marvers possession of ancient Lacrimian military armor. In response, Marvers removed the chest plate displaying the crest and packed it away. Waesstan appreciated the gesture and the three of them continued onward.\\n\\nAs the two men walked ahead of Ray, discussing the matter, Ray began to feel as though he was being watched, triggering a familiar anxiety. He did not hesitate to voice his unease and Marvers quickly understood exactly what he meant, they were being observed. By whom or what remained unknown, but Marvers recalled Commander Halden saying something that could point to the possibility that someone might be following the group.\\n\\nAs they continued, the party searched for a safe place to spend the night. They found a clearing near the main path, hidden enough not to attract attention from anyone passing by. Waesstan settled down and bantered with Ray while Marvers gathered materials for a campfire. Once the fire was prepared, Marvers suggested going hunting to distract himself. Ray initially wanted to join, but after Waesstan insisted they stay together, he remained behind. Marvers promised to return in about an hour, saying, “If I am not back in an hour, you can assume I am late.” With that, he ventured into the forest.\\n\\nAlthough he struggled at first, Marvers eventually managed to shoot an elk. The success brought back fond memories, which he briefly dwelled upon before slinging the elk over his shoulder and returning to camp.\\n\\nRay and Marvers skinned the deer together, with Ray showing Marvers the proper technique. Afterwards, they returned to camp and arranged the night watch schedule. Before everyone went to sleep, Ray recognized a song from his past that was just sung by Waesstan. Waesstan told Ray that it is an Ivian song and that he knows some of the dances from there. This lead to Ray dancing with Waesstan.\\n\\nThe feeling of being watched did not subside, and during the night, Marvers noticed two heads peeking out from a bush. At first, he assumed them to be small creatures like goblins, but they turned out to be two half elves, each a different type of spellcaster. The truth became apparent when one of them, panicked at being seen and attacked Marvers.\\n\\nA brutal combat ensued. Marvers struck down the older brother, enraging the younger sibling, who relentlessly attacked Marvers and knocked him down three times before finally being struck by Waesstan’s magical attack, finishing him off. \\n\\nAfter the battle, Marvers inspected the bodies and Waesstan noticed a crest on both elves armor. They bore the family crest of the noble Montmorency family, a pink crescent moon cradling a silver rose. “Grace endures where steel fails.” Thats what the family stood for. The Montmorencys were a secretive, strategic noble house in Lacrima, playing key roles in both the War of Scaled Nature and smaller conflicts with other countries. Outwardly loyal to the royal family, they nonetheless pursued their own influence behind the scenes.\\n\\nThe current heads of the house were Lord Thalanil Montmorency and Lady Sariel Montmorency, who had seven children: Endyl, Lirael, Caelwyn, Sylvaen, Caelyth, Orin, and Syvil. The two halfelves the party had struck down were Endyl and Orin, with Orin being the older brother. Upon inspecting the bodies, Marvers found gold, several weapons, and a letter on them. \\n\\"I shall be brief. Our informant has conveyed to us that the one now known as \\"Waesstan\\" makes his way towards Guardians Height. Should you encounter a circumstance that proves beyond your ability to manage, do not hesitate to withdraw. Fall back and summon assistance. No undertaking is worth risking your life.\\n\\nKnow that your mother’s concern mirrors my own. I place you in the care of Sune, hope you return unscathed from this operation.\\n\\nStay safe,\\nThalanil Montomorency\\"\\n\\nMarvers showed the letter to Waesstan and questioned him about the “Waesstan.” Waesstan confessed that he had previously gone by another name but, due to circumstances, had changed it.\\n\\nThe group stayed up for the rest of the morning and set out on their journey early. Along the way, they came across a small shrine dedicated to a fallen deity, one that Marvers had memories of from his past. This deity had been worshipped by one of his earlier companions. Seeing the shrine brought back memories of the last time he had seen her, when she had given Marvers her holy symbol after the deity had fallen. It was customary for followers of this deity to entrust the symbol to the most important person in their life to burn it as a signal that the era of belief had ended. She had asked Marvers to give it to the most important person in both of their lives: whether he had done so remained known only to him.\\n\\nAfter snapping out of the memory, Marvers took a quiet moment for himself and placed one of his rings on the shrine before the group continued on.\\n\\nA few hours later, the group arrived at the Stoneward Hideout, the outpost Commander Halden had sent them to. There, they were asked if they had a group name. Ray suggested “The Three Musky-tiers,” which was promptly shot down. The guards at the front gate allowed them entry and directed them to where they could find Commander Halden.\\n\\nInside the main building, the party found Commander Halden through a receptionist, who instructed them to go to Room 13. There, they saw Halden seated in a spacious room with an open fireplace and two red velvet sofas facing each other across a tea table. He was drinking tea and invited them to sit. He offered the party to stay for the night and continue the interrogation the next day. The party accepted the kind offer and dispersed, each taking some time for themselves before retiring for the evening.\\n\\nWaesstan remained with Commander Halden a little longer, as he had received a letter from him. They discussed some matters, during which Halden casually referred to his family as the “King’s Dogs” adding that he did not see himself playing that role. The exact meaning of his remark remained unclear.\\n\\nWith that, the party safely settled at the outpost.","highlights":["Being followed by Montmorency family members","The three Muskyteers"],"npcs":["Virex Halden","Montmorency"],"locations":["Lacrima","Guardians Height"]},{"id":"s04","number":4,"title":"Calm before the Storm at Stoneward Hideout","img":"/images/s4.png","date":"2026-02-02","summary":"The party arrived at the Outpost and after speaking with Commander Virex Halden, settled in for the night. Following a longer private conversation with the Commander, Waesstan returned to the assigned room to meet Marvers and Ray. There, Marvers openly shared his plan to visit the bathhouse. The idea of a warm bath appealed to Waesstan and he decided to join Marvers.\\n\\nMeanwhile, Ray chose to speak with Commander Halden about a sensitive matter. In exchange for Ray’s promise not to share the information with anyone, not even his companions, Halden revealed further details regarding the letters. Ray was also granted permission to use the Commander’s private bathhouse, where he bathed alone.\\n\\nWhile Ray enjoyed his solitude, Waesstan and Marvers relaxed in the mixed bathhouse. There, they encountered a noblewoman named Selene Witword. She spoke with Marvers about Duweil and praised the beauty of the kingdom. Selene recommended visiting the Festival of Deep Lights and warned that the main road to Duweil was closed, advising instead that they take an alternate coastal route. When Waesstan pressed her for more details about her noble status, she politely ended the conversation and bid them farewell.\\n\\nAfterward, Waesstan left before Marvers and went to the library to read. Ray soon joined him, though he appeared distant after learning a piece of information. Not long after, Waesstan departed the library and headed toward Commander Halden’s quarters.\\n\\nMarvers arrived at the library shortly after Waesstan left. He commented on how pleasant Ray smelled, which offended Ray, likely due to mounting stress. They talked it out and continued reading, but at one point Ray noticed Marvers becoming increasingly distracted. Without a word, Marvers suddenly left the library and headed outside.\\n\\nThere, he spent time instructing a young soldier named Samuel on improving his swordsmanship before stopping at the canteen, where he ate and drank himself into a fogged, sluggish state. Ray eventually returned to the room, calming himself by gazing at the stars through the window until he was interrupted by a very drunk Marvers. Ray helped him into bed, then retired for the night himself.\\n\\nWaesstan went to sleep much later, succumbing more to exhaustion than to any sense of restfulness.\\n\\nThe next morning, the group gathered for an interrogation. There, they learned the truth about Selene Witword and were questioned about their encounter with the Dragon on Guardian's Height. Afterward, they were promised a map to Duweil and sent on their way to the reception.\\n\\nAnd thats where the Session ended.","highlights":["Virex x Waess","Selene Witword bath scene"],"npcs":["Selene Witword","Marigold","Virex Halden"],"locations":["Lacrima","Stoneward Outpost"]},{"id":"s05","number":5,"title":"New Truths and saying goodbye to Lacrima, for now","img":"/images/s5.png","date":"2026-02-10","summary":"After the interrogation, the party made their way to the reception, where they received a map of Duweil from Marigold.\\n\\nMarigold explained that she couldn’t draw the route herself, as she had never been to Duweil. Because of this, Waesstan and Ray went to see Selene Witword to have the directions marked onto the map, while Marvers decided to stay behind with Marigold.\\n\\nWhen Waesstan and Ray arrived at the interrogation room, they found Selene sitting alone, surrounded by a pile of reports she still needed to complete. She greeted them warmly and gladly drew the route they would need to take. Selene recommended stopping at Thistlebrook along the way, suggesting they either purchase or borrow horses to make travel easier. Before leaving, Waesstan asked where he could find Commander Virex. Selene explained that Virex had left for duty and would not be at the outpost for the next few days. However, once the party reached Thistlebrook, Waesstan could send a priority letter that would reach Virex directly and immediately upon being sent. Selene also advised Ray and Waesstan to seek out the Magician to have their identification papers completed. Waesstan thanked her for the information, and he and Ray returned to the reception.\\n\\nMeanwhile, Marvers was speaking with Marigold after retrieving the party’s bags from their room. Their conversation started off a bit awkward but quickly became friendlier. Marvers revealed that he had once worked as a soldier in Lacrima, which sparked Marigold’s curiosity. She asked where he had been stationed, and Marvers told her he had served at the Royal Palace in Wiffprint. The discussion shifted to vacations and holidays, during which Marigold admitted that she had never taken a vacation herself, as she usually sent her money home to support her family in Wiffprint. Moved by this, Marvers gave her five gold and encouraged her to take some time off. In return, Marigold promised to send him a letter to PencePost, a large post office in Fooch.\\n\\nWhen the others returned, they asked about the Magician, and Marigold pointed them toward the canteen. There, they found a small elf, about 1.47 meters tall, wearing a black robe with purple stitching. Every Lacrimian wizard wore such a robe, with the stitching color indicating status, though none of the party knew what purple represented. The wizard, Serode, led them to the library and began the identification process.\\n\\nThe procedure involved asking a series of questions:\\n\\nName\\n\\nAge\\n\\nSpecies\\n\\nCitizenship\\n\\nBirthdate\\nTo verify the answers, Serode cast a truth spell. This caused a slight complication for Marvers and Ray, as both claimed to be human, which was not entirely true. In the end, everyone received their papers, though Marvers’s species was officially listed as “Dragonborn.” Both Marvers and Ray were more than confused about the reveal of their identity.\\n\\nOnce the paperwork was completed, Ray stormed out of the room, brushing past Waesstan and Marvers as he hurried to the reception to collect his bag. He then went to the interrogation room to ask Selene about rations and she directed him back to the canteen. There, Ray met a cook named Michael and asked him about coffee. Michael explained that coffee was a luxury item and difficult to acquire. Waesstan and Marvers soon joined Ray and Michael joked about traveling with Marvers before wishing the group a safe journey.\\n\\nAnd so, their travels began.\\n\\nAfter only an hour or two, the group reached the border, where panic set in as they remembered the chestplate from Marvers’s armor still in their possession. To make matters worse, Marvers admitted the issue with his identity papers. Despite this, they chose to proceed with a risky plan. Ray distracted the border soldier while Waesstan acted overly affectionate toward Marvers, clinging to him to get close enough to the chestplate and cast Redraw Rewrite on the crest. The maneuver succeeded and the group continued onward.\\n\\nAs night fell, the party settled beneath a large tree in a field of tall grass. Marvers went off alone to bury the chestplate, digging with his bare hands and injuring them in the process. When he returned, Ray helped bandage his wounds and prepared a stew using their rations. After eating, they set up a watch rotation and went to sleep. Ray fell asleep on his watch, luckily Marvers woke up on his own.\\n\\nDuring Marvers’s watch, he awoke to find four glowing eyes staring at him from the tree. This led to a fight against two bird like monstrosities. The party emerged victorious, but Marvers was infected with a condition known as Redding Ague. Ray rushed to him and cast Cure Wounds, healing his external injuries. Waesstan took over the final watch and the rest of the night passed peacefully.\\n\\nAnd that’s how Session 5 ended.","highlights":["Stoneward Outpost","Passport making gone wrong"],"npcs":["Selene Witword","Marigold","Virex Halden","Serode"],"locations":["Lacrima","Stoneward Outpost"]},{"id":"s06","number":6,"title":"Welcome to Thistlebrook","img":"/images/s6.png","date":"2026-03-04","summary":"After a big day out for Marvers (again), the group continued their travel. Marvers, not feeling that great, has expressed his thought of visiting a cleric to get himself looked at since a good night sleep did not help him recover from a strange exhaustion inflicting him. The party agreed that this was a good idea and after another day's travel they arrived at Thistlebrook.\\n\\n-> The the party approaches Thistlebrook, the road opens into a wide, calm village that feels lived in rather than fortified. The air is lighter here, carrying the smell of damp earth and salt from the coast. Thistlebrook is large by village standards and noticeably peaceful. Most of its inhabitants are Aarakocra and Water elves, moving easily between ground and sky.\\n\\nThe buildings are coated in muddy terracotta tones, rising vertically instead of spreading outward. The party immediately notices the dual entrances, lower doorways at street level and higher platforms, balconies and open archways meant for those who can fly. The village is washed in warm colors: reds, yellows, turquoise and oranges.\\n\\nNearly every home has shell and feather charms hanging near the entrances. They sway gently in the breeze, clicking softly as you pass, whether decorative, spiritual, or protective, it’s hard to tell. \\n\\nAt the center of Thistlebrook lies a massive open plaza. Market stalls are being taken down, merchants calling out, wings beating overhead as traders ascend into the sky.\\n\\nAt the Plaza there are 2 Statues, One is named \\"The Dragonslayer\\", it is a Statue of a Humanoid in full armor and a large Sword stamped to the ground. Next to is another Statue, also in Full armor, portaying Duweils military armor with he title \\"The Mudryy Chilavek\\"  <-\\n\\nThe party interacts with one of the traders whose name is Vurzus.\\nHe is a 64 year old male water elf merchant, his hair is a long pale green and partially braided.\\nHe has silky light blue skin and he stands about 170cm tall.\\n\\nThey ask Vurzus about Thistlebrook, his work, where they could aquire coffee and where the local church was. He happily answered all of the questions and got a bit intimidated by Marvers and his murderous Aura he gave off due to the exhaustion. \\n\\nThe Party bid Vurzus farewell and made their way over to the local church. When they arrive they find a Gothic style Church painted in bright colors. Murals of sea shells and water creatures decorate the exterior walls, its creation looking like a community project. At the entrance there was a long pearl and sea shell curtain that covered the entrance door. From afar it gave the illusion of a waterfall. When they entered they noticed the windows colourful stained glass shone brightly into the church. As their gaze wanders to the ceiling they notice a gigantic mural depicting a feast enjoyed by pixies and many other species.\\nThe Parties attention quickly shifted towards Sister Nelesh who stood at the back of the church. She greeted the three of them and asked how she can help them. They explained the situation to her and she agreed to examine Marvers condition. Waesstan and Ray then left for the Tavern and Inn, while Marvers stayed with Sister Nelesh. She brought him up to seperate room where a colourful persian rug from Ivia was placed down. She took of her shoes and pointed to the spot in front of her. Marvers sat down and she began with her assessment.\\n\\nWhile Marvers was left behind Ray and Waesstan made they way to Feathers & Fins. A large building placed on a plaza of its own. It strechted far into the sky. The bottom floor was build openly, water flowed through the entire tavern ground with seat cushions placed so that customers could hang their feet into the water. \\n\\nWaesstan and Ray chatted up the barkeep, Naelith who is also the owner of Feathers & Fins. There both Waess and Ray send of letters through her and also requested a room. Ray also went with her to check out the horses they could rent. \\n\\nShe introduced 3 horses that the party could also purchase if they took liking to the horse. Willow, Isla, Asher.\\n\\nRay made a comment on how \\"Marvers would fuck with that horse\\" and after Naelith gave him an off put look he realised that what he said could be highly misunderstood and proceeded to over explain himself into oblivion, making the situation more weird than it needed to be. \\n\\nThe both of them retreated back to the tavern. Waesstan flirted with the Hexblood bard before going up with Ray to check out the room. \\n\\nMarvers in the meanwhile got cured and asked where Sister Nelesh aquired the rug. Her answer  suggested than she purchased it at one of her pilgrimages in Ivia from possibly Marvers family. \\nShe gave Marvers a scarf from the same traders, asking for a favour in return and then let him go to meet up with his comrades. \\n\\nAt the tavern he checked out the bounty board where he found 2 Wanted posters of him, with one asking for 50 Gold to bring him alive and the other for 20 Gold to bring dead or alive. There was no name depicted, only a drawing that wasn't 100% accurate.\\n\\nWhen Marvers and the other two reunited he showed them the wanted poster. Waesstan exposed Ray of pulling Marvers into a conversation he was not part of, \\"He called you a horse fucker\\". Ray got drunk and cried about feeling guilty that he called Marvers a horse fucker. The conversation concluded in Marvers telling the guys that he agreed to do an escort job and Ray decided to follow him.\\n\\nWaesstan hit it off with the Bard, Rat, who also came from Lacrima.\\n\\nMarvers and Ray picked up Moltyn Zeghal, a noble who became a Cleric of Liira and went with her to the beach. There they had a jolly time before they were face to face with a elephant, turtle creature with elk antlers for its tusks.\\n\\nAnd thats how Session 6 ended.\\n\\nThe group has been traveling for 6 days.","highlights":["Thistlebrook","Feathers & Fins"],"npcs":["Sister Nelesh","Rat","Naelith","Moltyn","Vurzus"],"locations":["Duweil","Thistlebrook"]},{"id":"s07","number":7,"title":"The sickness is getting out of hand","img":"/images/s7.png","date":"2026-03-08","summary":"The session started with Marvers, Ray, and Moltyn running away from the Shellephant. All of them were hurt in some way as they tried to escape. Ray stayed behind for a moment to wait for Marvers, but the Shellephant attacked him and knocked him unconscious. Moltyn had already gotten far away, but when she saw what happened she ran back and healed Ray enough so he could stand up and run again.\\n\\nThe three of them managed to make it back to Thistlebrook. They went to the church and had some tea and coffee. While they were there, they asked Moltyn more about her noble background. She talked about things like tea parties and how boring they are.\\n\\nRay noticed that Moltyn seemed hurt from the escape and wanted to heal her disguised as a hug. Moltyn agreed to hug Ray but just before leaving the church, she gave the two of them 35 gold as payment for escorting her and said goodbye.\\n\\nRay hugged Moltyn and secretly tried to cast Cure Wounds, but it didn’t work. Moltyn noticed what he was doing and told him that he shouldn’t try to heal people without asking first. She said that next time he should just ask and that everything was fine.\\n\\nAfter that, Ray and Marvers returned to the inn and went to sleep.\\n\\nWaesstan woke up after his long night with Rat and before he left, said goodbye to Rat. He then went to check on his companions. He found Marvers and Ray asleep in the bed, with Ray completely soaked. Ray woke up as Waesstan joined them in the room and joked that he almost died but that Moltyn healed him. He and Waesstan agreed to talk about it later.\\n\\nWaesstan then went to get some medicine for Ray. After that he went to the market to buy something for Marvers. There he bought a golden ring with vines holding a small emerald.\\n\\nLater he went to the beach and sat in the sand. The sound of the ocean calmed him down and he started crying, letting some of the weight on his shoulders go with the waves.\\n\\nWhen he returned, he met Ray and Marvers again. He lightly asked them about Ray almost dying and they talked about whether they should take the other job as well. In the end they decided to take it.\\n\\nThey went to the church to ask Sister Nelesh for help or supplies. Next to her was a person completely covered up who could watch over the church while she was gone. Because of that, Sister Nelesh agreed to help the group.\\n\\nThey went to the roadblock and found a small pack of wolves. The wolves were acting strangely. The party soon realised that the wolves were sick with the same sickness the dragon carried. After defeating them, they warned Sister Nelesh. \\n\\nThey also told her that the sickness is present in Guardian’s Height, which is why the area is under quarantine. Waesstan shared that the sickness had spread in Lacrima already. Ray and Marvers were not aware of that and asked Waesstan why he had not shared that information with them and expressed that they would like that he would share something like this with them. Sister Nelesh examined the wolves and saw that the wound turned to ashen wood. She removed a small chunk and burned the other wooden parts in the field.\\n\\nWaesstan went back to the church and Sister Nelesh asked Ray and Marvers if they could bring the piece of wood and Moltyn to Fooch. Moltyn should be taken to Schiphra, Aarely's Mentor/follower of Soldea and the wood should be brought to the research center in Fooch.\\n\\nThe party said they would talk to Waesstan about it first.\\n\\nWhen they returned to the church, they found Waesstan upset. He told them it would be fine if they were angry at him and wanted to hit him because he held that Information from them. In his mind he wondered if he was just like the rest of his family after all. On the way to the tavern, Ray and Marvers tried to have a serious talk with Waesstan. But they realized that his problems couldn’t be solved with just one conversation. When they reached the tavern Marvers took a shower and headed down so Ray could take one aswell. Ray then went upstairs to take a shower, while Marvers returned and stayed with Waesstan.\\n\\nThe group has been traveling for 7 days. \\n","highlights":["Shellephant","Marvers new Ring","Sickness is spreading"],"npcs":["Lysha","Sister Nelesh","Moltyn","Naelith"],"locations":["Duweil","Thistlebrook"]},{"id":"s08","number":8,"title":"Disturbing truths","img":"/images/s8.png","date":"2026-03-17","summary":"The evening began quietly at Feathers & Fins, where Marvers and Waesstan shared a drink and easy conversation while waiting for Ray to finish cleaning up. Once reunited, the three made their way to the local church to meet with Sister Nelesh regarding the proposition: escorting Moltyn to the distant city of Fooch.\\n\\nTheir questions were practical ones, what exactly were they getting themselves into, were there any complications attached and what would the pay be? Sister Nelesh answered plainly. Moltyn, it turned out, is half construct. The sister offered two hundred gold for the job, one hundred upfront, the remainder upon safe arrival in Fooch, where the party would deliver Moltyn to a man named Shiphra, Aarely's mentor and a devoted follower of Soldea, leader of the Pale Sun.\\n\\nThe party accepted, but with one condition: Moltyn herself had to be willing. Sister Nelesh agreed to speak with her and it was arranged that Moltyn would come to the tavern with her answer.\\n\\nBack at Feathers & Fins, the mood shifted. Ray wandered to the back of the tavern and began rifling through the bounty board's stacked posters. Buried beneath the pile, he found one that gave him pause, old and worn, but bearing an eerily accurate portrait of Marvers, along with his name and a standing offer of three hundred gold for his capture. Alive.\\n\\nWhen the group gathered in their room to examine it more closely, Waesstan spotted something the others had missed: beneath the name \\"Marvers\\" nearly swallowed by time and faded ink, was another name, Fortis. The Fortis family was a noble house from Lacrima, known to have served the Royal family from the shadows. Not much else was known of them.\\n\\nMarvers said nothing. He stood, walked out of the room and didn't look back.\\n\\nHe nearly walked straight into Moltyn on his way through the tavern. She offered the church as a place to clear his head, he accepted without much deliberation, quietly asking Naelith not to tell his companions where he would go.\\n\\nLeft behind, Waesstan and Ray descended to the bar. Waesstan scanned the room with his usual optimism of finding someone to spent the night with but failed to find anyone of interest.\\n\\nAt the church, Marvers opened up more than he had in a long time. He told Moltyn the truth: that he fought in the War of Scaled Nature and that despite every appearance to the contrary, he is over four hundred years old. Moltyn, for her part, swore a pact of silence, to not tell anyone of the fresh information given to her.\\n\\nMarvers returned to the tavern and proceeded to get thoroughly drunk. Somewhere in the haze of it, talking with Waesstan, he let slip a comparison, something about an elven friend from long ago. The description landed. Waesstan went still. The friend Marvers described sounded unmistakably like Aasmias, his great uncle.\\n\\nThe two of them slipped away to talk properly and by the time Ray found them and joined in, the full weight of it had come out: Marvers had been married to the late King Astrad. He had spent approximately three hundred and eighty years imprisoned alone in a cell in Dredel, put there on the orders of the Queen, who he now wants dead.\\n\\nThe party sat with that for a moment. They agreed to help him. Then they went and got more drinks.\\n\\nAnd thats how the session has ended.\\n\\nThe group has been traveling for 8 days.","highlights":["Moltyn joins the Party","Marvers Secret","Aasmias"],"npcs":["Naelith","Serelis","Moltyn","Sister Nelesh"],"locations":["Duweil","Thistlebrook"]},{"id":"s09","number":9,"title":"Goodbye Thistlebrook","img":"/images/s9.png","date":"2026-04-04","summary":"The night gave none of them any real rest, only nightmares. Different, but just as bad. They all woke up around the same time and realised they had ended up huddled together in one bed.\\n\\nMarvers was the first to leave. He pulled away quickly and headed straight for the beach, as if he needed to get away. Waesstan stayed behind for a moment before going down to the bar, while Ray sat in the room, trying to calm himself and steady his breathing.\\n\\nAt the tavern, Waesstan sent a letter to Aasmias and got an unexpected reply. Inside was a key to a mansion in Fooch, along with news that Aasmias was heading to Kirkswell Ait and a warning about Marvers. Later, when Waesstan spoke with Naelith, she found out it was Waesstan's birthday. He was given a big portion of porridge and not long after, Ray also realised what meaning this big portion of porridge had.\\n\\nMarvers, in the meanwhile, had gone to the beach and dropped into the sand. Everything he had been holding in came crashing out. After a while, he walked into the water, going deeper until he couldn’t keep his head above the surface. Water filled his lungs and he quickly came to the realisation that the curse was more active than he first thought. He rushed back to shore, coughing and throwing up seawater, breaking down as he cried into the sand. The scars on his back burned as if they had just been reopened.\\n\\nRay went looking for him, stopping by the church first in case Marvers had gone there. He spoke briefly with Moltyn, then stepped outside and found Marvers standing there, completely soaked. They agreed to meet back at the tavern. Marvers made a quick change to his blood pact with Moltyn, then returned to Feathers & Fins.\\n\\nBack at the tavern, Marvers also sent a letter to Aasmias, including his thumb ring. After that, the group went to the market. There, Marvers ran into Lysha, the same woman who had sold Waesstan the ring he once bought for him. This time, Marvers picked out his own things: fabric that matched his pants, a ring that reminded him of Ray, an obsidian ring and some safety pins. Waesstan and Ray met up with him briefly to get a discount paper. Ray bought ale for Waesstan and cheese for himself.\\n\\nWhen they were done, they left the market, met up with Moltyn and set off for their first stop:\\n\\nPort Brightsear.","highlights":["Everyone had nightmares","Marvers almost drowns","Leaving Thistlebrook"],"npcs":["Naelith","Moltyn","Lysha"],"locations":["Duweil","Thistlebrook"]},{"id":"s10","number":10,"title":"On the road","img":"/images/s10 .png","date":"2026-04-04","summary":"The journey to Port Brightsear began with a clear order. Moltyn led the way at the front. Just behind her rode Ray and Waesstan, while Marvers kept to the back, quiet and distant.\\n\\nNot long after they set off, something strange happened. A small golem suddenly formed out of the saddle Waesstan was on, holding a tiny box. Inside was a letter, from his brother. The message was short, almost casual. It told him he had become an uncle.\\n\\nWaesstan did not take it well.\\n\\nThe news clearly upset him, more than he wanted to show. When Ray asked if he was alright, Waesstan admitted how frustrating it was, but quickly shut the conversation down, saying he didn’t want to think any further about it right now.\\n\\nAs they rode on, the group noticed a falcon circling above them. Ray recognized it almost instantly, Balzor, Erwin’s old hunting bird. The Common buzzard soon landed on Ray’s arm, a message tied to its leg. It was a letter from Erwin and Angel. Ray read it, paused for a moment, then wrote a short reply and sent Balzor back into the sky before continuing on.\\n\\nThe trip to Port Brightsear took about a week.\\n\\nDuring the first half, the group passed through a small stretch of forest, where they came across a pack of wolves attacking an injured weasel. They stepped in to help. Marvers killed one of the wolves, despite Ray clearly not approving of it. In the end, Ray saved the small white weasel and decided to take it with him. He buried the dead wolf before they moved on.\\n\\nLater, the land opened up and the ocean came into view. For a long stretch of the journey, the sea stayed beside them. They made camp on the beach one night, where Ray found a glass bottle with a message inside. He and Moltyn decided to write their own message and send it back out into the ocean.\\n\\nThat night was quieter. Marvers and Waesstan shared a rare, honest conversation. Not far from them, Ray and Moltyn spoke as well. At one point, Moltyn said something that stuck with Ray:\\n\\n“I guess you are always bound to where you are from.”\\n\\nThe words lingered.\\n\\nThe next days brought more trouble. The group ran into a gnoll chasing a wandering trader, someone who later proved to be quite annoying. The fight was short. The party took the gnoll down, with Ray finishing it by cutting off its head. On the body, they found a few truffle balls and some old, worn gear.\\n\\nThe trader introduced himself as A-L-D-R-I-C, a man in his thirties, with rough stubble and long brown hair tied back. Ray let him ride along on his horse for a while and with this very temporary companion, the group finally reached their destination:\\n\\nPort Brightsear.\\n\\nThe party has been traveling for 2 weeks. \\n","highlights":["Waesstan became Uncle","Ray rescued Misssnow","Gnoll encounter","A-L-D-R-I-C happened"],"npcs":["A-L-D-R-I-C","Moltyn"],"locations":["Duweil"]},{"id":"s11","number":11,"title":"Arrival in Port Brightsear","img":"/images/LacrimaBanner.png","date":"2026-04-05","summary":"The road dips and Brightsear reveals itself all at once. Off white stone walls catch the light, broken by weathered rooftops in terracotta, teal, and faded coral. The houses cluster tightly along the slope, as if the town simply grew there. As the party enters, the streets narrow into winding cobblestone paths, all slanting gently toward the sea. The air smells of salt, smoke, and cooking food. Laundry sways overhead, cats linger in doorways and no one seems to be in a hurry.\\n\\nThen the harbour opens below them, far larger than the town suggests. Ships rock gently in the water, ropes creak, gulls cry overhead and voices drift between dock and deck. It’s steady, alive… and easy to get lost in.\\n\\nUpon arrival, Moltyn takes the lead and heads straight for the stables to see to the horses and arrange a place for them to stay. The rest of the group regathers at the tavern, where they manage to secure one of the last available rooms, a small three bed space for 2 silver. With that settled, they make their way down to the market near the harbour.\\n\\nThere, the group splits up. Moltyn and Ray focus on supplies, picking up rations for the horses and food for Misssnow. They also stop at a stall offering flower stitching, asking for a lily of the valley to be added to Moltyn’s veil and a daffodil to Ray’s hat. Waesstan heads off to speak with a Triton sailor and successfully arranges a ride for later that night. Meanwhile, Marvers sells his deer hide before heading to the local smithy, where he meets a Dragonborn named Danryn. The two strike a deal, Danryn will craft a chestplate to complete Marvers armor for 10 gold. With that settled, Marvers returns to the tavern to wait for the Chestplate to be completed.\\n\\nAfter some time, Waesstan rejoins Ray and Moltyn and about an hour later they return to pick up their stitched clothing. It is there that things take a sudden turn.\\n\\nRay looks closely at the woman from the stitching stall.\\n\\nShe’s small, with tanned skin and thick black curls falling loosely around her shoulders. She wears a simple off white dress and white gloves. The moment she realizes Ray recognizes her, she moves quickly, grabbing his hand. Her lips form words, but no sound comes out. \\n\\"May the Graceful One take you and may the path he burns guide you.\\"\\nThen she presses a crumpled piece of paper into his hand and bolts.\\n\\nRay chases her without hesitation. It takes Waesstan and Marvers a moment to understand what’s happening before they follow after him. The pursuit is short, they lose her in the twisting side streets.\\n\\nShaken, Ray tells the others he’ll meet them back at the tavern and disappears into the crowd, asking around and searching for her. Eventually, he returns to the stall, where he finds Moltyn waiting. There, he discovers another note, this one clearly from the commune. \\"Now that you are an Advena, you have the freedom to walk around, but do not stray to far from the spot that has been assigned to you. After you have finished your job, you have one week to return.\\"\\n\\nMoltyn takes Ray out of the town, leading him to a quiet beach nearby. There, he tears the message the woman gave him into pieces and throws them into the ocean. The two talk for a while, Moltyn trying to calm him, Ray clearly shaken by what just happened. After some time, they return to Brightsear.\\n\\nBack in town, Marvers collects his finished chestplate from Danryn and invites him to the tavern later for drinks and cards. Waesstan meets Marvers briefly at the tavern before leaving again for his appointment aboard a ship called the \\"Dunedin Torch\\".\\n\\nMeanwhile, Ray and Moltyn continue searching for the woman. After some time, Moltyn manages to find her. Ray tackles her to the ground and presses a blade to her throat, demanding answers. She only grins. When she opens her mouth, the truth becomes clear, her tongue has been cleanly cut out.\\n\\nRay hesitates, but keeps the blade in place, until he realizes she is pushing herself against it. He lowers the weapon.\\n\\nMoltyn returns from the short space she gave the two. After hearing what happened, she reacts with anger, grabbing the woman and striking her before turning to Ray with a cold conclusion: they need to kill her. The two argue briefly, neither wanting it, but seeing no other option. Moltyn leaves to get Marvers.\\n\\nWhen he arrives, it ends quickly.\\n\\nMarvers snaps the woman’s neck, finishing with the words: “Your god has forsaken you.” In that final moment, she reveals one last thing, she had been able to use magic to communicate all along. Her final message, directed at Marvers:\\n\\n“He will come and take her back.”\\n\\nThe three of them hide the body as best they can and return to the tavern.\\n\\nRay goes upstairs to rest. Moltyn stays below with Marvers. Not long after, Danryn arrives and the two spend the evening playing cards. Later, Moltyn heads to bed and Waesstan returns, joining them briefly before also turning in for the night.\\n\\nMarvers, thoroughly worn down, is offered a place to sleep at Danryn’s smithy. He accepts and is half carried there before collapsing into a proper bed.\\n\\nAnd with that, the day comes to an end.\\n\\nThe party has now been traveling for 15 days.","highlights":["Arrived in Port Brightsear","Cult woman was killed by Marvers","Marvers made a new Dragonborn friend"],"npcs":["Cult Woman","Moltyn","Yenen","Danryn","Mara"],"locations":["Duweil","Port Brightsear"]},{"id":"s12","number":12,"title":"Continueing the Journey to Fooch","img":"/images/LacrimaBanner.png","date":"2026-04-11","summary":"After a restless night in the modest housing of Port Brightsear, the party awoke, each to varying degrees of comfort. Marvers, however, found himself in far better condition, having spent the night in Danryn’s home. There, he was treated to a warm breakfast, a soothing bath and genuine kindness. Before parting ways, Danryn gifted him a small bedroll and a heartfelt hug.\\n\\nThe group met at the tavern and wasted little time setting out once more.\\n\\nNot long into their journey, Moltyn called for a pause, urging the party to reflect on a recent event and ensure everyone was aware of the situation. They spoke of the woman they had killed in Port Brightsear and the danger that might now be pursuing Ray.\\n\\nAfter the talk, travel resumed and before long they encountered a deaf and mute girl, no older than sixteen or seventeen. Through gestures and a journal she had kept, she conveyed that her sister was gravely ill with an unknown disease and that the two had been abandoned because of it. In response, Waesstan used a scroll given to him by Aasmias to summon Selene. After a brief exchange, Selene agreed to help, opening a portal and taking both the girl and her sister to safety.\\n\\nWith that matter settled, the party pressed on.\\n\\nEventually, they arrived at their next waypoint: St. Moreeye. The village, usually a quiet refuge for travelers, stood eerily silent. No lights flickered in the windows and no souls walked the streets. The stillness was soon broken by the sudden attack of two infected gnolls, driven into a frenzy. The party defeated them, but what they uncovered next was far more unsettling.\\n\\nThe infection, referred to as Daphne, did not merely kill. It transformed. Those afflicted became ash colored, wood like trees, their forms twisted but hauntingly human. Upon closer inspection, faint facial features could still be discerned within the bark.\\n\\nInside one of the houses, Ray discovered a journal. It spoke of a missing “shipment” and a mysterious “flower branded visitor” who had tried to warn the villagers about the spreading sickness. One passage stood out:\\n\\n_“If we follow the Branded, we can be saved. Nobody listened. It spread.”_\\n\\nAfter reading it, Ray quickly took the journal and rushed outside.\\n\\nWith little left to uncover in the lifeless village, the party continued onward. Their path now leads them toward Fooch.\\n\\nThey have been traveling for 19 days.","highlights":["Leaving Port Brightsear","Talking about what happened","Disturbing discovery in St. Moreeye"],"npcs":["Sadra","Moltyn","Edrin","Danryn","Mara","Selene Witword"],"locations":["Duweil","St. Moreeye","Port Brightsear"]}]`);export{e as s};
